message: "Cite the EBAV working paper v0.1.0. DOI pending Zenodo archival."
title: "Evidence-Bound Adversarial Verification (EBAV): A Governed Field Method for AI-Assisted Software Verification and Release"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Coleman
    given-names: Brendon R.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://brendonrcoleman.com/methods/ebav/"
abstract: >-
  EBAV is a proposed seven-stage field method for evidence-bounded claims,
  immutable artifact preservation, independent adversarial software review,
  regression-driven correction, and separately scoped human authorization.
keywords:
  - adversarial software verification
  - AI-assisted software engineering
  - release governance
  - provenance
  - mutation testing
